From: immortalwrt-x86-fm350-pcie <noreply@local>
Subject: [PATCH] udp: validate packet length in socket GRO

Linux 6.6 validates the UDP length in udp_gro_receive_segment(), but the
socket GRO path in udp_gro_receive() can still accept a malformed UDP skb.
That skb can be completed as UDP fraglist GSO and later reach software
segmentation with invalid geometry, including a NULL frag_list.

Backport the early length check from upstream 8475a3efe6e6 using the helper
names available in Linux 6.6. Reject the skb before it can be aggregated by
the socket GRO callback.

Fixes: 9fd1ff5d2ac7 ("udp: Support UDP fraglist GRO/GSO.")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
---
 net/ipv4/udp_offload.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/net/ipv4/udp_offload.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/udp_offload.c
@@ -653,6 +653,12 @@ struct sk_buff *udp_gro_receive(struct list_head *head, struct sk_buff *skb,
 	struct sk_buff *p;
 	struct udphdr *uh2;
 	unsigned int off = skb_gro_offset(skb);
+	unsigned int ulen;
 	int flush = 1;
 
+	/* Do not deal with padded or malicious packets, sorry! */
+	ulen = ntohs(uh->len);
+	if (ulen <= sizeof(*uh) || ulen != skb_gro_len(skb))
+		goto out;
+
 	/* We can do L4 aggregation only if the packet can't land in a tunnel
 	 * otherwise we could corrupt the inner stream. Detecting such packets
 	 * cannot be foolproof and the aggregation might still happen in some
